  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nLet $A, B, C$ be three sets of complex numbers as defined below.\n$A=\\{z ; \\operatorname{lm} z \\geq 1\\} ; B=\\{z:|z-2-i|=3\\} ; C=\\{z: \\operatorname{Re}((1-i) z)=\\sqrt{2}\\}$.<strong>Question:</strong>\nLet $z$ be any point in $A \\cap B \\cap C$ and let $w$ be any point satisfying $|w-2-i| < 3$. Then, $|z|-|w|+3$ lies between"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$-6$ and 3\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-3$ and 6\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-6$ and 6\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-3$ and 9",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{array}{ll} \n& |w-(2+i)| < 3 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\quad|| w|-| 2+i|| < 3 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & -3+\\sqrt{5} < |w| < 3+\\sqrt{5} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & -3-\\sqrt{5} < -|w| < 3-\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{array}\n$$\nAlso, $|z-(2+i)|=3$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Rightarrow \\quad-3+\\sqrt{5} & \\leq|z| \\leq 3+\\sqrt{5} \\\\\n-3 & < |z|-|w|+3 < 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
